course: dictionary
lesson: 15737
title: Transmitted: sent, passed on, let through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Transmitted» comes from the verb «transmit», which means to send something from one place to another. The word has a few meanings, so use the clues around it. «The radio programme was transmitted live from the stadium.» Here the programme was sent through the air, so transmitted means sent out as a signal.
explain: Look at what is being passed along. «Flu can be transmitted when someone coughs near you.» The thing passed on is an illness, so transmitted means passed from one person to another. Now try the swap test: put «passed on» in place of transmitted and check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean letting something travel through a material. «Light is transmitted through clear glass.» Light passes through the glass, so you can see the trees outside. The clue is the word «through», which often tells you that something is travelling across or into a material.
fact: «Transmit» means to send something from one place to another.
fact: «Transmitted» means sent out as a signal, such as radio, TV, phone or internet.
fact: «Transmitted» can also mean passed on from one person or animal to another, as with germs or illnesses.
fact: «Transmitted» can mean let heat, light, sound or electricity pass through, as in «sound is transmitted through water».
fact: Clue words like «through», «by» and «from» often help you work out which meaning is used.
exercise: «The radio programme was transmitted live from the stadium.» What does transmitted mean here? | *Sent out through the air as a signal | Written in a book | Cooked in an oven | Painted on a wall
exercise: «Coughs can spread germs, so the flu is transmitted from person to person.» What is being transmitted? | A cold drink from the fridge | *An illness passed from one person to another | A song from a choir | A letter posted in a box
exercise: «Light is transmitted through clear glass.» What is the light doing? | Growing bigger and brighter | Stopping dead at the glass | Turning into a sound | *Passing through the glass
test: «The head teacher transmitted the news to every class.» What does transmitted mean? | Hid | *Passed on | Forgot | Stopped
test: «Sound is transmitted through water, so the whale's song travels far.» Where does the sound travel? | *Through the water, so it travels far | Only through thick walls | Only up into the sky | Only into empty space
exam: Which word best replaces transmitted in «The message was transmitted to every class»? | Hidden | Painted | Frozen | *Passed on
